R1 -- optical tidal matrix of the linearised metric (sympy, first order)
  T_yy = epsilon*(Derivative(Phi(x, y, z), (x, 2)) + 2*Derivative(Phi(x, y, z), (y, 2)))
  T_zz = epsilon*(Derivative(Phi(x, y, z), (x, 2)) + 2*Derivative(Phi(x, y, z), (z, 2)))
  T_yz = 2*epsilon*Derivative(Phi(x, y, z), y, z)
  trace T = 2 eps nabla^2 Phi (so traceless in vacuum, R_kk = 0)           ok trace=2*epsilon*(Derivative(Phi(x, y, z), (x, 2)) + Derivative(Phi(x, y, z), (y, 2)) + Derivative(Phi(x, y, z), (z, 2)))
  T - 2 eps Hess_perp(Phi) = Matrix([[epsilon*Derivative(Phi(x, y, z), (x, 2)), 0], [0, epsilon*Derivative(Phi(x, y, z), (x, 2))]])

R2 -- integrated transverse powers along the straight ray y = b (Phi = -M/r)
  P_yy (radial)    = -4*M_n/b**2
  P_zz (azimuthal) = 4*M_n/b**2
  P_yz             = 0
  azimuthal power = +4 M/b^2 (the alpha/b of the 4M/b deflection)          ok 
  radial power = -4 M/b^2 (-d alpha/db): astigmatic, trace 0               ok 
  radial power equals -d(alpha)/db, azimuthal equals alpha/b               ok 
  M sign +1: the focusing direction's power = 4|M|/b^2                     ok 4*M/b**2
  M sign -1: the focusing direction's power = 4|M|/b^2                     ok 4*M/b**2
  Born ray-map form 2 Hess_perp(Phi) integrates to the same P (infinite line) ok 

R3 -- thin-lens conjugate relation and the 'no real image inside f' criterion
  1/D_s + 1/D_i = 1/f  =>  D_i = f D_s/(D_s - f)                           ok 
  D_i > 0 iff D_s > f  (D_s < f: D_i < 0, virtual; D_s = f: D_i = infinity) ok 
  design point b = 0.3, M = 2e-3: f = 45/4 = 11.25 exactly                 ok 45/4
  D_s = 40: D_i = 360/23 = 15.6522 ; lambda_conj (from source) = 55.6522
  composite.py:52-53 prints lambda = 55.16 (M=+2e-3) and 56.52 (M=-2e-3)
  offsets from thin lens: -0.492 and +0.868 ; their mean +0.188
  D_s = 5 < f = 11.25: D_i < 0, no real conjugate point at ANY run length  ok D_i=-9

