R4b -- the fixed-b qualifier: the SAME point source at D_s = 5 seen through a smaller b
  b = 0.15: f = 2.8125 < D_s = 5 ; thin-lens D_i = 6.429 ; numeric conj at lambda = 10.949
  a source inside b^2/4M at b = 0.3 DOES form a real conjugate point through b = 0.15 ok 
  => 'a source inside f forms no real image' holds for the rays at THAT b, not for the lens

R6 -- the only physical datum: PPN gamma in alpha = 2(1+gamma)M/b  => f = b^2/(2(1+gamma)M)
  VLBI, Barcelo-Visser gr-qc/0003025 eq.5.52 (as restated there): |df/f| <= |gamma-1|/2 + 3 sigma/2 = 4.9e-04
  gamma at its measured value moves f = 11.25 by < 0.01 (source-5 margin is 6.25) ok 5.57e-03
  composite.py's metric is GR by construction (gamma = 1): no datum enters its focal length

